PART 7 — COMBO ASSIST AND COMBAT ASSIST WORKING TOGETHER

23. Preserve Combat Assist as a separate feature

Alva’s Combat Assist can close a small gap before executing a melee attack.

It is human-player-only and enabled by default.

It does not cost Energy.

It does not extend attack hitboxes or teleport the fighter.

It should remain a separate setting from Combo Assist.

A player should be able to use:

* Neither assist.
* Combo Assist only.
* Combat Assist only.
* Both assists together.

All four combinations must work.

24. Queued follow-ups must integrate with Combat Assist

Example:

The player successfully performs Attack 1.

The player repeats Attack 1 to queue Attack 2.

Attack 1 completes.

Attack 2 is a melee move, and the target has moved just beyond its natural reach.

If Combat Assist is enabled and its normal conditions are satisfied, it may start its ordinary short approach before executing Attack 2.

This must use Combat Assist’s existing measured range, collision restrictions, facing logic, travel limits and airtime rules.

Do not grant a special extra-long approach because the move came from Combo Assist.

Do not teleport the fighter into range.

Do not give it free extra air dashes.

Do not apply Combat Assist to projectiles, homing attacks, techniques, summons or other excluded moves.

If Combat Assist is disabled, the attack must use its normal range and may miss.

Both assists should complement each other, but neither should override the other’s restrictions.

25. Handle Combat Assist’s active approach state

Combat Assist has its own in-progress approach state before the actual attack begins.

During that approach, the attack animation is not yet playing.

A repeated button press during an approach must not be mistaken for a repeat during the eventual attack animation.

Preserve the existing approach-replacement and cancellation rules.

The queued follow-up should become available only when a real attack is actually active.

If an approach is canceled before its attack starts, do not leave a future combo queued for an attack that never occurred.

