FINAL DIRECTIVE

The ultimate purpose of this update is to solve an important fighting-game usability problem:

Players should not feel that pressing a button was pointless merely because they pressed it slightly earlier than an animation ended.

At the same time:

An attack should never restart, cancel itself, or bypass its recovery simply because the same button was pressed again.

Alva already has the building blocks: fixed-step input, an ordinary input buffer, individual cooldowns, manual cancellation, Combat Assist, and Combo Assist.

Connect them carefully.

A beginner should be able to press Attack 1 twice and understand what happens.

An experienced player should still be able to perform deliberate attack cancels and advanced combos without the assist getting in the way.

A fighter’s animations, cooldowns and mechanical identity must remain trustworthy.

Make Alva more forgiving without making it automatic, more responsive without making it chaotic, and more satisfying without destroying its depth.

Implement the update completely, verify it thoroughly, and deliver a clean, maintainable result.
